  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nSubtropical high pressure will lift into the lower Mississippi River \nValley Tuesday and Wednesday while upper low pressure enters the \nFour Corners region. This will amplify the southwest flow over Iowa. \nDespite this evolution, the Gulf Moisture stream will be veered to \nthe southeast of Iowa as surface high pressure moves into the \nNorthern Plains. This is trending precipitation chances southward \nTuesday and Tuesday night. The greater chances for precipitation are \nlater in the week from Wednesday night into Thursday as the main \nupper level system lifts out of the southwest. Temperatures will \ngradually cool through this period as well. Broad northerly flow \nwill follow the upper system passage and usher a cooler, fall like \nairmass into to Iowa for the end of next week.",
